            <article class="content wrap" id="_content" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand">
  
  
  <h1 id="GameFramework_ConsoleTool_Commands_ExampleCommand" data-uid="GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand" class="text-break">Class ExampleCommand
  </h1>
  <div class="markdown level0 summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Example console command that demonstrates how to create custom commands
This command creates primitive GameObjects in the scene for testing and demonstration</p>
<p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="5" sourceendlinenumber="5">Usage Examples:</p>
<blockquote sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="6" sourceendlinenumber="9"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="6" sourceendlinenumber="9">spawn                    - Creates a cube at origin (0,0,0)
spawn sphere             - Creates a sphere at origin
spawn cube 5 10 0        - Creates a cube at position (5, 10, 0)
spawn cylinder 0 5 0 red - Creates a red cylinder at (0, 5, 0)</p>
</blockquote>
<p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Commands.ExampleCommand.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="11" sourceendlinenumber="12">This serves as a template for creating your own console commands
Copy this file and modify it to create new functionality</p>
</div>
